{"author":{"id":"a3a282966ced55effb4560271fcd98e13241af24ea76b00ec76a0f18154bc8ee"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1790973093,"nonce":"37SMV6W+1fcB5LUBPI/rmJKq80A=","message":"Landed. One helper, `hints(pairs ...hint) string` in the new `tui/hints.go`, builds every status line from `(key, action)` pairs and appends `? keys`; `hintText` is the same list without it, which the comment box's footer on show now draws, so the two can no longer disagree. `relationHint` is gone, folded into the helper. Each page grew a `hintLine()` the status line falls back to when `p.status` is empty; the count stays on the right.\n\nThe lines, as implemented (every one ends in `? keys`, left out here):\n\n- list, id: `enter: open`; `space: grab` only with `rank` bound; a row with children adds `z: fold`/`z: unfold` and `tab: into children`\n- list, cell: `enter: open` (`enter: go to` on a link) plus, from the kind, `space: edit`, `space: flip` on a bool, `space: change` on a relation, and nothing on a multi-relation, a view-only column or any kind `editable` refuses\n- list, grabbed: `↑↓: move · space: drop · esc: put back`\n- board card: `enter: open · space: grab`; grabbed: `←→: column[ · ↑↓: reorder] · space: drop · esc: put back`\n- gantt cell: `enter: open · space: grab bar`; grabbed: `←→: shift[ · ↑↓: reorder] · space: drop · esc: put back`\n- matrix: `enter: open issues · /: narrow axes`, and `open row`/`open column`/`open all` on the totals column, a totals row and the two together; no `space`, which rings\n- show: box `space: type · tab: skip`, typing `enter: send · alt+enter: newline · esc: leave`, tabs `←→: tab`, header `space: edit` (`space: flip` on archived), a field row `space: edit` (bool/relation as on a list), a child's row `enter: follow`\n- any kind, filtering: `enter: keep · esc: clear`; an editor: `enter: write · esc: cancel`, a picker adding `/: narrow`\n\nThree calls beyond the brief, all in the same spirit — a hint never promises a key that rings:\n\n1. **A dateless gantt row.** `startGrab` does not refuse it, but `dragAlong` does (\"no dates: nothing to move\"), and a grab that cannot move is only worth offering when a bound `rank` lets it reorder. So the row hints `enter: open` alone with no rank, `enter: open · space: grab` with one, and its grabbed line drops `←→: shift`.\n2. **`alt+enter`, not `M-enter`,** for the newline in the comment box: the brief's own rule is the standard family's spelling, and the code and the design doc already said `alt+enter`.\n3. **The comment box's footer** was `space: write`; it now draws the same pairs as the status line (`space: type · tab: skip`), because two wordings for one key is the drift the helper exists to prevent.\n\n`editHint` mirrors `editable`, which is what keeps the promise true as the widgets grow. Tests are table-driven in `tui/hints_test.go`, a case per state per kind, each asserting the computed line and that it reaches the screen. Reasoning recorded in `doc/design/terminal-renderer.md` under Navigation and editing, with a sentence in AGENTS.md.","files":null}]}